[31m-### Component Breakdown[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Device Discovery (UDisks2 D-Bus)**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The extension connects to the system bus and calls `GetManagedObjects` on `org.freedesktop.UDisks2` to enumerate all block devices. It filters for devices where:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-1. The parent `Drive` interface has `Removable == true` and `ConnectionBus == "usb"`[m
[31m-2. The block device exposes an `org.freedesktop.UDisks2.Filesystem` interface (i.e., it is mounted)[m
[31m-[m
[31m-It subscribes to `InterfacesAdded` and `InterfacesRemoved` signals to dynamically track USB hotplug and mount/unmount events without polling D-Bus.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**I/O Monitoring (`/sys/block/<dev>/stat`)**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Every 2 seconds, the extension reads the kernel's block-layer statistics for each tracked device. The relevant fields from `/sys/block/<dev>/stat` are:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Field Index | Name              | Description                            |[m
[31m-|-------------|-------------------|----------------------------------------|[m
[31m-| 4           | writes completed  | Total completed write requests         |[m
[31m-| 6           | sectors written   | Total 512-byte sectors written         |[m
[31m-| 8           | in-flight I/Os    | Currently queued I/O operations        |[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Partition names (e.g., `sdb1`) are automatically resolved to parent disk names (e.g., `sdb`) since `/sys/block/` only contains whole-disk entries. This resolution handles SCSI/USB (`sdXN`), NVMe (`nvmeXnYpZ`), and MMC (`mmcblkNpM`) naming schemes.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Two-Phase Write Detection**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A per-device state machine prevents false positives from small metadata writes (journal commits, inode updates, directory entries) while maintaining indicator visibility during legitimate file copy operations:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Phase 1 -- TRIGGER (strict thresholds)**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Both conditions must be met simultaneously to start tracking a write burst:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Delta bytes >= 64 KB per tick (~32 KB/s at 2-second polling)[m
[31m-- Average I/O request size >= 16 KB[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Small, frequent writes typical of filesystem metadata will not pass these thresholds.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Phase 2 -- SUSTAIN (permissive)**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Once triggered, any write activity (even small sector changes or in-flight I/O) keeps the indicator alive. This prevents the indicator from flickering off during gaps between kernel writeback rounds.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**DONE (idle detection)**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The burst ends only after 5 consecutive idle ticks (10 seconds) with zero sector changes and zero in-flight I/O. This generous grace period accounts for the bursty nature of Linux's writeback mechanism.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-              +------------------+[m
[31m-              |     IDLE         |[m
[31m-              | (indicator off)  |[m
[31m-              +--------+---------+[m
[31m-                       |[m
[31m-                       | large write detected[m
[31m-                       | (>= 64KB/tick AND >= 16KB avg I/O)[m
[31m-                       v[m
[31m-              +------------------+[m
[31m-              |    WRITING       |[m
[31m-              | (indicator on)   |<---+[m
[31m-              +--------+---------+    |[m
[31m-                       |              | any activity or[m
[31m-                       |              | in-flight I/O[m
[31m-                       |              |[m
[31m-              +--------v---------+    |[m
[31m-              |   IDLE TICK?     +----+[m
[31m-              | sector_delta==0  |[m
[31m-              | && in_flight==0  |[m
[31m-              +--------+---------+[m
[31m-                       |[m
[31m-                       | 5 consecutive idle ticks (10s)[m
[31m-                       v[m
[31m-              +------------------+[m
[31m-              |     DONE         |[m
[31m-              | notify + reset   |[m
[31m-              +------------------+[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Indicator (Top Bar)**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A `PanelMenu.Button` with a USB drive icon and a dynamic label. Hidden when no writes are active. When one or more devices are writing, the label shows:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-DEVICE_LABEL: 123.4 MB (5.2 MB/s) · DEVICE_2: 45.0 MB[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- Total bytes written in the current burst[m
[31m-- Live write speed (updated each tick when new data arrives)[m
[31m-- Multiple active devices are separated by ` · `[m
[31m-- Speed display is suppressed when a device is in a writeback gap (shows only total)[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Notifications**[m
[31m-[m
[31m-When a device transitions from WRITING to DONE, a desktop notification fires:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-> **USB Sync Complete**[m
[31m-> Write cache flushed -- safe to eject DEVICE_LABEL.[m
[31m-[m
